WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.170
"Benefits and Side Effects of the Shingles Vaccine"

00:00:07.237 --> 00:00:09.120
Adult vaccination
can be thought of

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.340
as a cornerstone
of successful aging,

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:12.780
but a major issue

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.180
hampering the uptake
of shingles vaccination

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.880
is the lack of awareness
of the disease.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.820
Shingles is caused
by a reactivation

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.740
of the chicken pox virus
later in life.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:25.500
After your body
beats back chicken pox,

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.380
the virus hides in waiting
in your spinal cord,

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:31.260
waiting for an opportunity
to strike back.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.080
When it does,
the virus can surge forth,

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.300
traveling along the path
of a nerve

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.320
branching off the spinal cord,

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.540
wrapping around one side
of the body to the front,

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.880
producing skin blisters
along the way

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.740
in a characteristic
belt-like pattern

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.320
that does not cross
the midline in front.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.040
Both shingles and the name
of the virus, zoster,

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.680
are from the Latin and Greek,
respectively, for "belt".

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.740
The blistering rash
can be intensely painful

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.020
and leave scarring
or discoloration behind,

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:00.600
but usually disappears
in a few weeks on its own.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.200
However, approximately 30
to 50 percent of people suffer

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.940
"postherpetic neuralgia,"

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.720
persistent pain that can last
for a year or more,

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.700
that sometimes
can be debilitating.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.820
Usually, it affects nerves
around your trunk,

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:17.220
but in 10 to 25 percent
of cases,

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.380
it can erupt across your face,

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.200
which can lead to permanent
facial muscle weakness,

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.960
hearing loss,
or blindness.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.240
As if that's all
not bad enough,

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.600
having shingles as much
as quintuples your odds

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.540
of having a stroke
over the subsequent few weeks,

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.220
a risk that gradually declines

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.260
over the following
six to twelve months.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.620
It's surprising more people
don't know about it,

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.860
since the lifetime risk
of shingles is 30 percent.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:46.140
Meaning nearly one in three
will get it

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.280
sometime in their lives.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.700
Young adults only have
about a 1 in 1,000 chance

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:51.660
of getting it every year,

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:53.460
whereas in older adults

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.520
that climbs to closer
to 1 in 100 each year.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.520
That comes out
to a million cases of shingles

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.200
every year
in the United States.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:04.140
Thankfully,
there is a shingles vaccine.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.900
The first became available
in 2006,

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.360
using a live weakened strain
of the virus.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.420
The efficacy
was only about 50 percent

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:15.720
and couldn't be used in
immunocompromised individuals,

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:19.020
such as those with HIV
or on immunosuppressive drugs,

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:20.640
such as many on chemotherapy.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.260
Thankfully, in 2017,

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.960
a recombinant
shingles vaccine was approved

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:29.280
with a 90 to 97 percent efficacy
for preventing an outbreak.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.380
It requires
two separate injections

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.520
2 to 6 months apart,

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.980
and is expensive,
like 280 bucks,

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:36.360
but covered by Medicare

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.760
and most private
insurance plans.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:41.460
It also can cause
transient systemic symptoms,

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.740
such as muscle aches,
fatigue, headaches,

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.840
or fever and chills
serious enough to interfere

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.660
with everyday activities
about 10 percent of the time,

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:51.000
but the new vaccine
is considered

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.700
so much more effective
that it's recommended

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.380
for everyone
starting at age 50,

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:58.740
even if you were previously
immunized with the old one.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:02.340
Given that the new vaccine
is only about five years old,

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:05.820
longer-term safety
and efficacy data

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:08.340
is still coming in,
but, so far so good.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:12.000
As soon as I turned 50,
I lined up for mine.

